# Shows LoginPage's dev-only "Continue as ..." buttons in a built (non-local) deployment.
# import.meta.env.DEV alone only covers `vite dev` — it's always false in a production build,
# so a deployed Dev-tier environment would otherwise have no way to sign in until real SSO
# (Section 13) is wired up. Set to "true" ONLY for the Dev-tier build config — never
# staging/prod, since these buttons bypass authentication entirely.
VITE_ENABLE_DEV_LOGIN=

# The backend API base URL and real SSO (Entra ID / Azure AD) values are NOT env vars — Vite
# bakes VITE_* vars in at build time, but these must be injectable per-environment at DEPLOY
# time without a rebuild, and never committed to the repo. See instead:
#   public/config/appsettings.config.json       — local dev placeholder (committed, empty)
#   charts/auditiq-frontend/appsettings.config.json — Octopus fills this in at deploy time
#     (#{Api.BaseUrl}, #{AzureAuth.ClientId}, etc.) into the deployed copy nginx serves at
#     /config/appsettings.config.json
# src/config/runtimeConfig.ts fetches whichever copy is live at app startup. Leaving api.baseUrl
# blank means "same origin" (local dev's Vite proxy handles routing /api to the local backend).
# Leaving clientId/tenantId blank means "SSO not configured yet" — the app falls back to the
# dev-login flow above.
